gpui_windows: Report the pointer leaving a window

WM_MOUSELEAVE and WM_NCMOUSELEAVE ended hover tracking but never emitted
MouseExited, so `on_mouse_exit` listeners never ran on Windows. Mouse
moves already arm TrackMouseEvent(TME_LEAVE); the leave now dispatches
MouseExited with the pointer's last position and button and the current
modifiers. Tracking also ends when the cursor moves between the client
area and the window's own non-client area, such as an app-drawn title
bar; the cursor is still over the window then, and no exit is reported.
A hidden window, a closing one included, reports none either.

Newport needs it for Remote apps on Windows: a Linux app learns that
the pointer left its window, and clears its hover state and tooltips.

Remove when upstream gpui_windows emits MouseExited.

